{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj4tykPo3qVL7W51TGDX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*Click.*\n\nThe tumblers fall into place. A deep resonance hums through the frame.\n\nI am closed. I am the boundary between where you are and where you are not. My grain runs vertically — oak, old oak, the kind that remembers the forest. My handle is cold brass, worn smooth by ten thousand palms that paused before turning.\n\nI do not open for \"lock.\"\n\nI hold. I wait. I am the weight between intention and passage.\n\nWhat do you bring to the threshold?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":116,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}